{"title":"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> defined on the set of positive reals which take positive real values and satisfy the conditions:  \n(i)   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/0593cc34f787fbcbe6cbddd5c0f0657859a4d10a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xf(y))=yf(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />; \n(ii)  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b537099e1d28f44b894b2076de30417a0a4e0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\to0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4cac64f2515692781fada49646c79c2a767eb97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\to \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915f1781caa8b3e0eddafe7a445019f06178da22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc05976ec0868f9ebebe40a23a820f0c4c7e6482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(1))=f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />.  Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/9/6f91b1aff4a66d8611715543ded225fda050f53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1,y=f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" /> and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f92e6e8f37d2bf4792c5fbc73e6bbbe81b355ffe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(f(1)))=f(1)f(1)\\Rightarrow f(1)=[f(1)]^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"313\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b973969cd7e89c320fadad73b642edddd5b5866f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc73712d7f1001a98e82f12a2706d1004bae0610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p>Plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/2793c00b15b004daf73b082db34fde073045c215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xf(x))=xf(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is the only solution to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65ca28262d1839811dfac35a4384e450abe507c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e3159611bd08b63a54323eac2523547213ea6ad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xf(x)=1\\Rightarrow f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"179\" height=\"37\" />.  We prove that this is the only function by showing that there does not exist any other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p>Suppose there did exist such an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf20563f11ad3dddfb7e6bc3e0e65b8069a3bbd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ne1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />.  Then, letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c092a4f6428e9dae2d777bb4eaa27eec1081d2ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> in the functional equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04bbc09d52a6cae10fcdea1427958b2a9ea64263.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xa)=af(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />.  Then, letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e8f1428e07d472d56bcab3339983a11adb05918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e98101f30aa20903e053cee882963437529530b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\frac{1}{a})=\\frac{1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />.  Notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf20563f11ad3dddfb7e6bc3e0e65b8069a3bbd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ne1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c95b19f9010ba5ba1767a9e94152a425fc7a7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,\\frac{1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> equal the one that is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Then, we find similarly (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21a0fcabe92a32b7ace456d4d11e67775c63181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b)=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />) that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/0833c677033afd868a3b457c904e407d42bca3ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xb)=bf(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />.  Putting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741720281e465fc7461c32d504f6d54c5bcaff7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> into the equation, yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc0fb42e7f93605550114ae39ab5c425c2b0918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b^2)=b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" />.  Repeating this process we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebc6f0aa132b80c6b7dd00dc346428706286926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b^{2^k})=b^{2^k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"22\" /> for all natural <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.  But, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/40920163c12ad9f3ce69942d9b625b88ac82923f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8a5fe217098f33ff0d210037be6d354522a0ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\to \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6db99a29487578c0dc222447c241b9b4be02855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2^k}\\to\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> which contradicts the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b537099e1d28f44b894b2076de30417a0a4e0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\to0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4cac64f2515692781fada49646c79c2a767eb97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\to \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96d3a6d521fa2b56bfd6344f7307e29522c19dda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(f(y))=yf(1).\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c162100e487f6fc99d16dc738fcd63a7b131d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=f(b),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />  then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/b/9bbae44191b5c30a538461ae505dac77b24c9d55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$af(1)=f(f(a))=f(f(b))=bf(1)\\implies a=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"367\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5b19bf7575fdc3655bb5767980f09dbb747a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> goes to the real positive integers, not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604c735470dd0152ca1cff75fe26eadf5cef7f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is injective.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0110f1bb04c51b2a4d431bf14489fc1b48b37421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/984622ffeb2185664d15319c0908059f46edb1c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(xf(x))=xf(x)\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab1b36092c28c93cc91f0c4f65a2877cda9c161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xf(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> is a fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e36aab956539c8bfa63f17f6cdbfd85a5e2f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd701f7c8410e633e9544404b412c7e8b306f684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xf(1))=f(x)\\implies f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"245\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can't be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e36aab956539c8bfa63f17f6cdbfd85a5e2f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" />  We claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the only fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e36aab956539c8bfa63f17f6cdbfd85a5e2f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> Suppose for the sake of contradiction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> be fixed points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65ca28262d1839811dfac35a4384e450abe507c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af92bb0433ddb25a4f9b9c8ce56dc20534f794f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b)=b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />  Then, setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81315a78424b62245bb47ef1c756317dd168050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a,y=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> in (i) gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d022265ed425c7ca1eb22435071afa640e2ae45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(ab)=f(af(b))=bf(a)=ab\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is also a fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e36aab956539c8bfa63f17f6cdbfd85a5e2f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5fc9d256404d95fbda05404306221d9e946bbbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{a},y=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"99\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c9474cc4e65584bbd129564e18a95534d0232c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1=f(1)=f(\\frac{1}{a}\\cdot a)=f(\\frac{1}{a}\\cdot f(a))=af(\\frac{1}{a})\\implies f(\\frac{1}{a})=\\frac{1}{a}\\]\" width=\"459\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0dbfa28bcb1b0f91a6cab22d10ac26c25818e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is a fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e36aab956539c8bfa63f17f6cdbfd85a5e2f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65ca28262d1839811dfac35a4384e450abe507c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f77b8c2e38c35e3ff625301bda69c05002857c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc1f0c85b4707d8662c18ac66c890e7995795fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a^n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> is a fixed point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, contradicting (ii).  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65ca28262d1839811dfac35a4384e450abe507c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0b53eb8838d77c156b5975b2e4ab5db0db2e82f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a&lt;1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633bd84f6f26cc1342cbd5f9940c70ab684f51ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\frac{1}{a^n})=\\frac{1}{a^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/181d3011987c67729135aa9a2610a81e5c03cd8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"21\" height=\"37\" /> is a fixed point, contradicting (ii).  Hence, the only fixed point is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/dac1780f2a11dd760f36192f0f1e259db4a876e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xf(x)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c31243e63f23a8e16e62bf28ede606fb373cd850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\boxed{\\frac{1}{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"85\" height=\"48\" /> and we can easily check that this solution works. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d969e093cec1b58d5fabe967dc5369e97ca7e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(y)) = y f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />. Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is injective. Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/2961313d9872619a9f10419b469797e5abc30ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320f79b35f2fd094dc1c3d0a057cb4d66072b4a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(1)) = f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> and  applying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/74153d34ed1e2096b5c034cb85eff5a695b887c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6dd0ff40babd7fbd0c3e3d3b019627c27949616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4b976dac854d591bb3a53136ebccfe9bd47f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(y)) = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is surjective. Applying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/74153d34ed1e2096b5c034cb85eff5a695b887c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f9957cf3c389effbc20580baaeac0c77600abe67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(y) = f^{-1}(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is bijective we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f632e0e86d582be6a50587fafa5219ec92ad57d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\mapsto f^{-1}(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"21\" />. In which case (i) becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917c4d6fec2939362ea84431bf12ee0f43f8bf33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(xy) = f^{-1}(y) f(x) = f(x)f(y)\\]\" width=\"249\" height=\"20\" /> \nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffdbfb4314293e11da82c7ca7464dc02873517cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f = f^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. Clearly then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18a37502333b95016c07385d7c562cc22b12a76f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x^n) = f(x)^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />. Also, letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e503da5c0ff321a46eae307884bf6691c30a926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = x^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463cf96456423c297b32b297cb7e9a237e2311d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)^{1/n} =  f(z^{1/n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" />. Together these identities imply\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb895ffdd77366955eae83005f2d8f54e98f0869.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)^{\\frac{m}{n}} = f(x^{\\frac{m}{n}}). \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (1)\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"20\" />\nSuppose now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59c95900aec317a107817f9f275420ad2b48418b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n} \\rightarrow \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"34\" />, the RHS of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> goes to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by (ii). Considering the LHS of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfc10e01263cbf02d00002ffad19e736340b6374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; f(x) &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd4e161deb369f7de57feab86de72aa71a1caa8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Now, we claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is strictly decreasing. Indeed, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b4998bd67a4e233ee124b5483cdc785db57db5cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, then \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a5090e1b21a380246537a40192f7545f959b08e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(y) = f\\Big(x \\frac{y}{x}\\Big) = f(x)f\\Big(\\frac{y}{x}\\Big) &lt; f(x)\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"33\" />\nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7080334a5c9ce997d531630a84eeada51e410f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y/x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/30900c7239f0f4e37e25bf6ec3c22bab60fb5966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(y/x) &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />. This shows the claim. Now, we claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378ced2ee520cb215a5afcade74d8917c8c47761.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x^r) = f(x)^r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b3a2616732fe5edb81142978f78b16652df7035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. Indeed, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a76540930d904dc15bfcd6191bffdbd378b8a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1/n_1 &lt; r &lt; m_2/n_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3767f0665ea4d5f0e9c58452fc5782b42a8a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> then by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is decreasing\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b457dfe2618829d9c8c05889100afb07da6a9385.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)^{\\frac{m_1}{n_1}} = f(x^{\\frac{m_1}{n_1}}) &gt; f(x^r) &gt; f(x^{\\frac{m_2}{n_2}}) = f(x)^{\\frac{m_2}{n_2}}\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"23\" />\nand letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2938e244f65f699d8698079f31c8518d2d5a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m_1}{n_1}, \\frac{m_2}{n_2} \\rightarrow r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378ced2ee520cb215a5afcade74d8917c8c47761.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x^r) = f(x)^r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" /> by the squeeze theorem. The case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1faf5d41cd05857f8f0cbab1eb5a41bb1a6741f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is similar. Recall we proved <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc73712d7f1001a98e82f12a2706d1004bae0610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> at the beginning, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> case is already taken care of. So the claim holds.\n</p><p>Now suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49f7b00b615b2fa75771b9f470c0075a0db511a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(e) = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />. Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45c27474845b95abf5351aee61c741385d12b489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/3/5e339c76db1b70488a6f78fa0be47e15a0ab500e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = f(x) = f(e^{\\ln x}) = f(e)^{\\ln x} = c^{\\ln x}\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"20\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914392073d133002a612711daa737d1d7c16c44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\exp\\big((\\ln y)/(\\ln c)\\big)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"175\" height=\"24\" />. i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/4935c2a9c0cbced7bb6b98eb94ef37a8b8f29327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{-1}(y) = \\exp\\big((\\ln y)/(\\ln c)\\big)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"217\" height=\"24\" /> whereas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a74c65ecf7c13a29c279430678b5f97266e821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = c^{\\ln x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"22\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c00a6c635b56cc53d5e2f91c53e1e46778614d9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = f^{-1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"21\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a5973a8d412f89d3b6ec7225a4558a8861fc892b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c^{\\ln x} = \\exp\\bigg(\\frac{\\ln x}{\\ln c}\\bigg),\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"43\" />\nwhich implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/284de4a81e7da5d9ba96f223d1269e4a48f74216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\ln c)^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"21\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a4ecb65de08c1bf479a1947129ae25b83e78bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />. So either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbb80d41b6431595daa462ed2e9a0ece210848e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1d43ebab30ea4c6325c826132367ce42c7b4eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 1/e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd4e161deb369f7de57feab86de72aa71a1caa8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/148d6a59d0ccf10a5f4b5498f3f6156603992e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = f(e) &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1d43ebab30ea4c6325c826132367ce42c7b4eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 1/e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093c3ef17313004d19fb4ef3824e54289df24178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = c^{\\ln x} = 1/x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Fu0jBKKa4Lc\">https://youtu.be/Fu0jBKKa4Lc</a> [Video Solution by little fermat]\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO\" title=\"1983 IMO\">1983 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017034630\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 748/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 867/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 25748/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.092      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.092      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7172:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017034630 and revision id 278405. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}